3. ስንክሳር (SYNAXARIUM)
   Both editions — መጽሐፈ ስንክሳር በአማርኛ and መጽሐፈ ስንክሳር በግእዝ, 366 days each —
   were scanned from available PDF scans of the printed books by the Sinq
   maintainer, who releases them as open content under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0, the
   same terms as the bundled Bible text. Built by tools/build_sinksar.py.
   The underlying commemorations are traditional Ethiopian Orthodox
   liturgical content.

   The text is reproduced as the scans carry it, with three disclosed
   exceptions: each paragraph's number is written twice in the source, once
   in Arabic and once in Ge'ez, and only the Ge'ez is kept (all 18,764 of
   them agree, which the generator re-proves on every run); editorial
   dingbats and stray markup are removed; and two Ge'ez days that carry no
   heading block are given one naming their date.

   Earlier releases of Sinq bundled the Amharic synaxarium from the
   gitsaweandsinksarbot project by hailemariam-eyayu
   (https://github.com/hailemariam-eyayu/gitsaweandsinksarbot) and the
   Nexuss0781/synaxarium dataset on the Hugging Face Hub
   (https://huggingface.co/datasets/Nexuss0781/synaxarium). Neither is
   bundled any longer.

4. ሥርዓተ ማኅሌት (MAHLET)
   The orders of service are merged from three books. The spine is
   ሥርዓተ ማኅሌት ዘዓበይት በዓላት and the ዘመነ ጽጌ አቋቋም volumes, scanned from available
   PDF scans of the printed books by the Sinq maintainer; the six orders those
   do not carry come from the ግጻዌ credited below and are labelled with it.
   Released as open content under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0. Built by
   tools/build_mahlet.py.

5. ግጻዌ (GITSAWE)
   The lectionary (the fixed 366-day cycle plus the movable, Sunday,
   Athanasius, and Bahre Hasab collections) was scanned and transcribed from
   the printed ግጻዌ by the Sinq maintainer, who releases it as open content
   under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 — the same terms as the bundled Bible text. The
   underlying lectionary is traditional Ethiopian Orthodox liturgical
   material.

